From 1db039c78bec62b8b29e13da9fe900881e29420c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Van Tran <tetcu@fgorg.vn>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:50:37 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(decisions): structured decisions on issues: API, issue
 panel, CLI

- feat(decisions): structured decisions on issues

  Table issue_decision (add-only, no foreign keys): a question, 2-8 options
  (at most one recommended), due date, who asked (member or agent), and the
  answer. API: list/create on an issue, answer (people only) and cancel,
  plus GET /api/issues/decisions/open for the workspace. Waiting is enforced by
  the workflow gate; clients post the answer as a comment so the usual
  triggers wake the agent. Workspace deletion removes decisions.

- feat(decisions): decision panel on the issue page

  Open decisions show above the approval panel: the question, the options with
  the recommended one marked and preselected, an optional note, and Answer.
  Answering records the choice and posts it as a comment so the issue's agent
  wakes up. Core: @multica/core/decisions and client methods.

- feat(decisions): CLI for agents

  multica issue ask <issue> --question --option (2-8, "Label|description")
  --recommended --due opens a decision; multica issue decision list <issue>
  | --open and decision cancel <issue> <id>. Agents talk to Multica only
  through the CLI, so without it they could not ask. No answer command:
  the server lets only people answer.

Patch-Id: decisions
